{"run": "digest", "t": 44482, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Business and economy] The Japanese finance ministry says it spent a record ¥15.4 trillion (US$96 billion) between July 30 and August 26 to support the yen, marking the country's largest monthly currency intervention on record."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 44482, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Health and environment] Seventh cholera pandemic — Nigeria records 65,000 cases of cholera, across 35 states, alongside 10,000 cases of diphtheria. Additionally, NCDC director Jide Idris reports a decline in cholera cases but also warn that transmission of cases remain ongoing."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 44482, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] Corruption in Ecuador — An Ecuadorian court convicts former president Lenín Moreno of bribery linked to the construction of the Coca Codo Sinclair plant in Napo Province. His wife, Rocío González Navas, and daughter are also found guilty."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 44482, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] Scam centers in Cambodia — The Cambodian government says that they have closed more than 700 online scam centers and arrested nearly 30,000 suspects, including 15 senior officials and law-enforcement officers, during a year-long crackdown on cybercrime networks."}
